---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for Bug Days - Learn how we handle your data and protect your privacy."
  keywords="privacy policy, data protection, Bug Days privacy"
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-800 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 p-6 md:p-8">
      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-8">Last updated: September 15, 2026</p>

      <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6">

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Overview</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            Bug Days ("we", "our", or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard information when you use our website at bugdays.com.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Developer Tool Data</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            Most conversion, formatting, and diagnostic tools process their input entirely in your browser. For those tools:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Your data is processed locally on your device</li>
            <li>Tool input is not sent to Bug Days</li>
            <li>Tool input is not stored by Bug Days</li>
            <li>Bug Days cannot recover input that remains only in your browser</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
            Tools that perform network operations are exceptions. The IP lookup and access-log analyzer send only extracted, unique IP addresses to the Bug Days lookup API; raw logs, paths, headers, query strings, and user agents stay in the browser. API clients send requests to the endpoint you choose, directly or through a local bridge when selected. Each applicable tool explains its data flow on the page.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
            Sharing is explicit. URL shares place compressed report data in the address fragment. If you choose short-link storage, the share payload is sent to Bug Days and retrieved by its identifier. Review a report before sharing it because recipients can see the data included in that report.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Analytics - Google Analytics (GA4)</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            We use Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to understand how visitors use our website. GA4 collects:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Pages visited and time spent on pages</li>
            <li>Device type, browser, and operating system</li>
            <li>Approximate geographic location (country/region level)</li>
            <li>Referral source (how you found our site)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
            GA4 uses cookies and similar technologies. This data helps us improve our tools and user experience. Google's privacy policy can be found at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Advertising - Google AdSense</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            We use Google AdSense to display advertisements on our site. AdSense may use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to our website or other websites. You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Contact Form</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            If you use our contact form, we collect the information you provide (name, email, message). This data is stored securely and used only to respond to your inquiry. We do not share this information with third parties.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Cookies</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            We use the following types of cookies:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Essential cookies:</strong> Used to remember your preferences (e.g., dark mode setting)</li>
            <li><strong>Analytics cookies:</strong> Used by Google Analytics to understand site usage</li>
            <li><strong>Advertising cookies:</strong> Used by Google AdSense to serve relevant ads</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Data Retention</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            IP lookup requests are processed to return matches and are not stored as lookup records by the application. URL-fragment shares are not stored by Bug Days. Short-link payloads, contact submissions, and analytics data are retained according to their applicable service and operational policies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Your Rights</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            Depending on your location, you may have the following rights:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
            <li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
            <li>Object to or restrict processing of your data</li>
            <li>Data portability</li>
            <li>Withdraw consent at any time</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
            To exercise these rights, please <a href="/contact/" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 hover:underline">contact us</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            We use the following third-party services:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Website analytics</li>
            <li><strong>Google AdSense:</strong> Advertising</li>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> Content delivery and security</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
            Each service has its own privacy policy governing their data practices.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            Our services are not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the "Last updated" date.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-slate-100 mb-3">Contact Us</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please <a href="/contact/" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 hover:underline">contact us</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
